# mutgap2_rdec_primitive_type_10: Primitive type 10 in every draw form mutgap_dec_render_primitive_type_10 leaves out: 0x00, 0x01, 0x03, 0x05, 0x06, 0x07, 0x08, 0x09, 0x0a, 0x0b, 0x1c, 0x1d, 0x10 and 0x11 each check the primitive type, which throws "Invalid primitive type", a decode error: the exec's command buffer is never committed (docs/testing.md, 6.12), so neither the blit fill in its first segment nor the pass's clear lands. exclusive: a draw that reaches Metal with type 10 faults the GPU (render_draw_type9).
